{
  "turn_number": 2,
  "player_text": "I keep my voice low and don't take the coin back yet. \"Who saw those footprints, and how long ago? Did anyone from the gate actually go look, or is this just travelers talking?\"",
  "visible_motivation": "The runner just tied the missing patrol to muddy footprints northwest of the crates and said that spot is worth watching.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want to know how fresh and reliable the footprint rumor is before I act on it.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "\"From what I gathered,\" the guard captain says quietly, \"several gate guards spotted those footprints just this morning near the crates northwest of the entrance. A couple of them were sent out to investigate, but they came back without word—no sign of the patrol or what became of them. So far, the talk you're hearing is mostly rumors swirling among travelers and refugees, patchy and unsettled.\" They glance toward the muddy approach, their expression tight. \"If you want answers, the northwest track past the crates is where to start looking.\"",
  "generation_attempt_2": "The guard captain narrows their eyes, considering your questions carefully. \"No one from the gate watch has actually gone to inspect those footprints yet,\" they say quietly. \"Locals and travelers passing through noticed them earlier this morning near the northwest crates. The timing matches when the patrol last checked in before disappearing. If you’re thinking of investigating, that’s the direction to head.\"",
